From 527c1f8da9a5aefadfc0d9d43f37383d04032f43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:15:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] config: upgrade direct dependencies and their compatibility
 fixes

Upgrade direct dependencies and port their APIs while retaining the six documented compatibility holds.

Refs: holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed#71
Base: openai/codex rust-v0.163.0 (83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012).
Prerequisites: issue 60 and earlier release-queue patches documented in README.md.

The current registry audit covers 252 direct crates. Before the final lock refresh, five additional AWS/wildmatch direct dependencies trail stable; after targeted cargo update only the six documented holds remain. Bazel lock regeneration succeeds and reports existing jemalloc/libgit2 annotation diagnostics. Full platform validation remains required.

Regenerate two rules_rust extension fingerprints with Bazel 9.3.1.

Refresh direct BCR modules to llvm 0.8.25, rules_rs 0.1.3 and rules_cc_autoconf 0.29.0. Rebase the Windows MSVC linker and execution-root separator patches while retaining upstream equals-delimited path redaction. Maintained Bazel 9.3.1 lock regeneration passes; native platform behavior remains a release gate.

Advance the isolated argument-comment linter and its packaged Dylint commands to 6.2.0 together. Pinned nightly tests pass with -Dwarnings: five library tests (including nine UI cases) and three runner tests. Driver and toolchain caches are confined to project build caches. Bazel lock regeneration passes; existing native annotation recommendations remain separate warning-policy work.

Select Tokio 1.54.1 because RUSTSEC-2026-0384 affects the yanked 1.54.0 release. The registry dependency and feature contracts are identical; update its Cargo checksum and Bazel crate fact together. The maintained Bazel 9.3.1 lock check passes. Cargo Deny no longer reports RUSTSEC-2026-0384; advisories covered by later security patches still require full-queue verification.
